---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who Dee Tater is and why this site exists.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <em>Sample bio — placeholder copy. Replace it with your own in src/pages/about.astro.</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m Dee Tater. I’ve spent most of my working life building software and small companies,
        and most of my free time reading about how other people did the same. This site is where I
        think out loud.
      </p>
      <p>
        There are two kinds of writing here. <a href={url("/essays/")}>Essays</a> are slow: I rewrite
        them until they say something I’d still agree with in five years. <a href={url("/notes/")}
          >Notes</a
        > are fast: a lesson from this week, a passage from a book, a half-formed idea worth keeping.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write mostly about <a href={url("/tags/startups/")}>startups</a>, <a href={url("/tags/engineering/")}
          >engineering</a
        >, <a href={url("/tags/reading/")}>reading</a>, and <a href={url("/tags/life/")}>life</a>. If something
        here was useful — or wrong — I’d like to hear about it.
      </p>
      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a></li>
        <li>Feed: <a href={url("/rss.xml")}>RSS</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
